 atmosphere, calmness, decision quality, technical competence, but communication difficulty, egocentric, unwillingness to further education. Candidate B's stress resilience, technical competence, but weak memory for numbers, nasty remarks, pretentious tone.\n\nAgent 2's own notes: B: very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, pretentious tone, relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about colleagues. C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, also we have from other agents: 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, excellent attention skills.\n\nWe need to respond to Agent 1's reaffirmation of C. We could either agree and reinforce, or raise a new concern. Perhaps we could bring up the egocentric and unwillingness to further education as more serious than B's memory issue? Or we could ask about B's memory impact. But we need to give a vote. Likely we keep C.\n\nWe should reference Agent 1's points and maybe add that C's egocentric attitude could affect crew cooperation, but overall reliability and crew atmosphere outweigh B's memory and attitude issues. Provide explicit facts: \"100% reliable\", \"creates positive atmosphere\", \"keeps calm in crisis\", \"can make correct decisions quickly\". Also note B's \"relatively weak memory for numbers\" and \"makes nasty remarks\". Conclude we still recommend C.\n\nThus public message: agree with Agent 1, reinforce C, mention concerns but weigh them.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
