n crisis, understands complicated technology, excellent attention, difficulty communicating, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nWe need to decide. The panel seems leaning toward C. As Agent 3, we could either defend B or reconsider. The instruction says we should be open to being convinced. The evidence for C is strong across many criteria, while B has serious concerns about memory and nasty remarks. The earlier argument from Agent 3 emphasized B's stress resilience and technical competence, but now we have more evidence about C's reliability and crew atmosphere. Also we have Agent 2's note about B's weak memory for numbers and nasty remarks. That is a serious safety concern. So perhaps Agent 3 should reconsider and shift vote to C.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: mention Agent 2's points about B's weak memory and nasty remarks, and Agent 1's points about C's reliability and crew atmosphere. Provide explicit facts: B \"relatively weak memory for numbers\", \"makes nasty remarks about colleagues\". C \"100% reliable\", \"creates positive atmosphere with crew\", \"keeps calm in crisis\", \"can make correct decisions quickly\". Then explain why C outweighs B's strengths. Conclude we now recommend Candidate C.\n\nThus we will change vote to Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C."}
